	<name>Aloha Social</name>
	<summary>Aloha Social puts your Nextcloud on the fediverse</summary>
	<description><![CDATA[Aloha Social is a social network inside your Nextcloud. The people on your server get an account that talks to the whole open social web, and their posts, pictures and videos stay on a server you run.

- **On the fediverse:** follow and be followed by people on Mastodon, PeerTube, Pixelfed, Misskey and every other ActivityPub server, and they can follow you back.
- **A Bluesky host of its own:** the administrator can make this server a Bluesky host, so every account here can also be on Bluesky, with a handle under your own domain.
- **Works with your apps:** Mastodon apps on phones and desktops sign in to it once the web server forwards the API at the domain root (the rules ship in contrib/webserver), and so do Bluesky apps when Bluesky is on.
- **Timelines:** your home feed, this server, the wider network, photos, videos, lists, hashtags you follow and bookmarks.
- **Posting:** replies, polls, content warnings, up to ten pictures, videos or sound files with alt text, a language, a time to publish later, and edits with their history.
- **Quote posts:** you decide who may quote each of your posts, and can take a quote back.
- **Reactions:** likes, boosts and emoji reactions, with counts hidden until you choose to see them.
- **Direct messages** with people here, on the fediverse and on Bluesky.
- **Videos and shorts:** a Videos timeline that includes the PeerTube channels you follow, a watch page, shorts you keep on your profile and shorts that are gone after a day.
- **Discover:** people to follow, starter packs, trending hashtags, and For You, a feed that learns from what you like and follow, if you turn it on.
- **Your privacy:** location and camera data are removed from photos, and blocking, muting, word filters and a notification policy keep out what you do not want to see.
- **Moving made easy:** bring your follows and posts over from another server using nothing but your old handle, and take your follows, blocks and lists with you when you leave.
- **Part of Nextcloud:** share pictures from Files, link cards in Talk, Text and Deck, Activity entries, dashboard widgets, unified search and notifications.
- **For administrators:** reports, a review queue for new accounts, block lists, relays, server rules, custom emoji, statistics, and setup checks in Administration → Overview.
- **Open to guests if you like:** the administrator can let people without a Nextcloud account register for Aloha Social only, by invitation, with approval or openly.

Aloha Social implements ActivityPub, a large part of the Mastodon client API and the AT Protocol. It is not a drop-in replacement for a Mastodon server; the documentation lists what is supported.]]></description>
